93171.4 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap declared=50 visible=46 resolved=50 missing=0 first=CP_SUNSHINE/NATURE/BLENDROCKTOGRASS001 resource=materials/nature/rockwall009_height-ssbump.vtf reason=the materials name 23 distinct $bumpmap textures, so the one sampler slot the pass started with cannot apply each material's own; per-material binding is the --world-material-bump switch, and with it on the 30 that do not set $ssbump sample their own tile through a texinfo-axis tangent basis while the 20 that do stay refused (see the $ssbump row)
93171.5 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap2 declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 first=- resource=- reason=-
93171.5 gpu: world feature feature=ssbump declared=20 visible=19 resolved=20 missing=0 first=CP_SUNSHINE/NATURE/BLENDROCKTOGRASS001 resource=nature/rockwall009_height-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
93171.5 gpu: world feature feature=detail declared=56 visible=52 resolved=0 missing=56 first=WINTER/ROCKWALL014 resource=materials/Overlays/detail004.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused
