93265.2 gpu: world lighting-control control=dynamicLighting kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=136 triangles=52502 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant, not a material key: the pixel shader replaces the lightmap-only factor with 0.62+0.38*dot(normal, lightDirection) for 136 visible materials / 52502 visible triangles; no VMT declares it, so every surface is shaded by the same guessed direction and the baked lightmap's own direct light is counted twice; off
93265.2 gpu: world lighting-control control=specular kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=136 triangles=52502 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant: one lobe (boost 0.12, exponent 32) for 136 visible materials / 52502 visible triangles; no visible material declares $phong, so the lobe is added to materials that never asked for one; off
93265.3 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=50 visible=46 resolved=50 missing=0 materials=46 triangles=32769 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=CP_SUNSHINE/NATURE/BLENDROCKTOGRASS001 resource=materials/nature/rockwall009_height-ssbump.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 46 visible materials that name one of 23 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
93265.3 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=not-declared declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=0 triangles=0 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=no material declares $bumpmap2
93265.3 gpu: world lighting-control control=%detailtype kind=material-key state=refused declared=56 visible=52 resolved=0 missing=56 materials=52 triangles=21575 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=WINTER/ROCKWALL014 resource=materials/Overlays/detail004.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused; 56 of 56 referenced detail VMTs are absent from this install, so the layer's own texture and blend mode cannot be resolved here; %detailtype is a key in the material that names the layer, not in the detail VMT, and is read above; 2 materials name a %detailtype group (first=tf_forest_grass_lowdensity); %detailtype names a detail-prop group that VBSP consumes at map compile time (it emits prop_detail sprites and models there), so the key never reaches a runtime shader and has no consumer here
